{
  "title": "Memos \u2014 note-taking, knowledge management, social (59,886\u2605)",
  "content": "Project: Memos\nDomain: note-taking, knowledge management, social | Scale: medium | Stars: 59,886\nProblem: Provides a lightweight, self-hosted note-taking solution for quick capture with total data ownership. Designed as a privacy-focused alternative to cloud-based note-taking apps, eliminating telemetry and vendor lock-in.\nTarget users: Privacy-conscious individuals, Self-hosted infrastructure enthusiasts, Knowledge workers needing quick note capture, Teams wanting data sovereignty\nCore features: Instant Capture with Timeline-first UI; Markdown-native note editing and storage; Multi-database support (SQLite, MySQL, PostgreSQL); REST and gRPC APIs for integration; Self-hosted deployment with Docker/Kubernetes; AI integration (OpenAI, Google Gemini); S3-compatible storage backend\nIntegrations: OpenAI API, Google Gemini, AWS S3, Docker, Kubernetes, gRPC, OAuth2, Model Context Protocol (MCP)\nTech stack: React with TypeScript + Go (Echo framework, gRPC) + SQLite, MySQL, PostgreSQL + Docker, Kubernetes, Docker Compose\nKey libraries: connect-rpc, grpc-gateway, goldmark (Markdown), echo (HTTP framework), aws-sdk-go-v2, openai-go, google/genai, mcp-go\nArchitecture: microservices\nDesign lessons:\n- Lightweight single-binary deployment (20MB Docker image) prioritizes accessibility and reduced operational overhead for self-hosting\n- Polyglot backend with gRPC and REST APIs enables ecosystem extensibility while maintaining simplicity for basic use cases\n- Data portability through Markdown storage and zero telemetry reflects privacy-first design principle as core differentiator\n- AI integration via plugin architecture (OpenAI, Gemini, MCP) allows feature expansion without core bloat",
